      "severity": "critical",
      "narrative": "IAM privilege escalation via Lambda function creation with a privileged execution role. A principal with sts:AssumeRole reaches a role that has iam:PassRole + lambda:CreateFunction + an invocation vector. The principal assumes the intermediary role, creates a Lambda function passing a high-privilege execution role, and invokes it — the function runs with the execution role's full authority. This is a two-hop path: AssumeRole → PassRole+CreateFunction → admin. Documented in Rhino Security's CloudGoat (lambda_privesc) and Bishop Fox's IAM Vulnerable. Threshold 1: detection of either hop alone is sufficient to flag the path.\n Failing: CTL.IAM.ESCALATE.PASSROLE.CREATEFUNCTION.001.",
